# Demo Authoring

Demo files are plain HTML consumed by `cem serve` for live component previews.

## File Structure

```html
---
description: "Short sentence describing what this demo shows."
---
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/flotsam.css">

<flotsam-example variant="primary">Hello</flotsam-example>

<style>
  /* Demo-specific layout styles only */
</style>

<script type="module">
  import '@flotsam/elements/flotsam-example/flotsam-example.js';
</script>
```

## Rules

- YAML frontmatter `description` is required — it appears in the CEM docs UI
- Always link the shared token stylesheet: `<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/flotsam.css">`
- Import elements as ES modules via the `@flotsam/elements/` path
- Import only the elements used in this specific demo
- `index.html` is the primary/default demo for the element
- Additional demos use descriptive filenames: `sizes.html`, `variants.html`, `responsive.html`
- Keep demo markup minimal — show one concept per file
- Demo-only styles go in an inline `<style>` block, not in the component CSS
